# Live-Isaac-

Live-Isaac is a lightweight live chat app built to give users a quick way to enter a conversation and stay active for a short session window. The experience is intentionally simple: users can join, chat in real time, and the session ends after three minutes.

## Features

- Real-time chat using Socket.IO
- 3-minute session countdown
- Live presence tracking
- Simple browser-based interface
- Easy local setup

## Tech stack

- Node.js
- Express
- Socket.IO

## Run locally

1. Install dependencies
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

2. Start the app
   ```bash
   npm start
   ```

3. Open the app in your browser
   ```text
   http://localhost:3000
   ```

## How it works

- The app opens a live chat room for a short session.
- Users choose a display name and join.
- Messages are broadcast instantly to everyone in the room.
- The room closes after 3 minutes and the session resets for the next round.

## Project status

This is a working MVP and can be expanded with authentication, persistent storage, private rooms, or a database-backed chat history.
